## 1. Introduction
In the early 20th century, certain metal salts were found to be capable of regulating the catalytic activity of metal catalyst in reduction reaction of aldehyde.[1-2] Since then, research on metal promoters in the field of catalysis has been extensively explored, especially in supported metal catalysts.[3-5] To date, the metal promoters with the capability of regulating the acid-base properties, electronic state or surface structures of catalysts, can improve their catalytic activity, selectivity or stability in various reactions such as water gas shift, Fischer– Tropsch synthesis, ammonia synthesis, Suzuki coupling reaction, and battery electrode reaction.[6-13] Due to these crucial roles, the study of metal promoters remains a research hotspot.
Currently, there are mainly three categories of metal promoters in catalytic system. One is the direct addition of metal salts or metal complexes as metal promoters into the reaction solutions, most of which are dispersed in the solution and only few are absorbed on the catalyst surface.[14-15] Typically, zinc ions as metal promoters are introduced into Rucatalyzed benzene hydrogenation system to boost the selectivity toward cyclohexene.[16-17] However, due to the complicated forms of metal promoters, not only the recovery of metal promoters is difficult, but more importantly, to elucidate the real action mechanism behind metal promoters faces challenge. Secondly, it is widely used to introduce metal promoters
