present similar characteristic peaks with bpy-UiO, indicating the negligible impact of the introduced Cu promoters and loaded Pd NPs on the crystal structure of pristine Pd/bpy-UiO, as evidenced by X-ray diffraction (XRD) measurements (Figure 2d). As shown in the highresolution transmission electron microscopy (HRTEM) images, the loaded Pd NPs are evenly distributed onto the bpy-UiO carriers (Figure S5), as well as that in Pd/bpy-UiO-Cu catalyst (Figure 2b and Figure S6). As revealed by HRTEM and corresponding inverse fast Fourier transformation (IFFT) images of one individual metal NP, a lattice distance of 2.23 Å corresponding to (111) lattice plane of Pd NPs is also observed (insert in Figure 2b and Figure S7), which further confirms the formation of Pd NPs. In addition, the introduced Cu promoters are well dispersed in Pd/bpy-UiO-Cu catalyst, as demonstrated by the elemental mapping images (Figure 2c), indicating that Cu promoters are successfully introduced into Pd/bpy-UiO matrix.
