To explore the interaction among bpy-UiO support, Cu promoters and Pd NPs, XPS measurements were conducted to show the electronic structure of $\mathrm{Pd}/$ bpy-UiO-Cu catalyst (Figure 4a). After inserting single-site $\mathrm{Cu}$ promoters, the $\mathrm{Pd}3d$ binding energy of Pd/bpyUiO-Cu ( $340.2\mathrm{eV}$ for $3d_{3/2}$ and $334.9\mathrm{eV}$ for $3d_{5/2}\mathrm{\cdot}$ ) shows slightly higher values $(+0.2\ \mathrm{eV})$ than that of Pd/bpy-UiO $340.0\mathrm{eV}$ for $3d_{3/2}$ and $334.7\mathrm{eV}$ for $3d_{5/2}$ ) (Figure 4b), and the Cu $2p$ binding energy of Pd/bpy-UiO-Cu ( $934.3\mathrm{~eV}$ for $\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$ and $932.3\ \mathrm{eV}$ for $\mathrm{Cu}^{+/0}$ ) shows
